---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Drop from "../components/Drop.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";

const draftTowns = [
  "Brookline",
  "Beechview",
  "Banksville",
  "Carrick",
  "Overbrook",
  "Baldwin",
  "Brentwood",
  "Whitehall",
  "Dormont",
  "Mt. Lebanon",
  "Castle Shannon",
  "Bethel Park",
];
---

<Base
  title="Service Area"
  description="Coulehan Plumbing LLC is based in Pittsburgh, PA 15226 (Brookline) and works around the South Hills. Neighborhoods are still being confirmed with the owner."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow"><Drop size={16} /> Service area</p>
      <h1>A Pittsburgh plumber, based in 15226.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Coulehan Plumbing LLC is in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania 15226. That ZIP is
        Brookline, on the south side of the city. The work described on the
        current site is local: residential and commercial plumbing. Serving
        Pittsburgh since 2014.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" >
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>South Hills, around Brookline</h2>
        <p>
          15226 sits in the South Hills, among the neighborhoods south of the
          rivers. That is the honest center of the map until Jerry names the
          towns he wants on the site. Nothing below is a promise that every
          one of those places is in the service area.
        </p>
        <p>
          One Facebook post is outside that circle. Jerry wrote that he helped
          the West View / Ross Township community install three new toilets at
          a baseball field. The sign in those photos reads Scharmyn Field. That
          is a job he described. It is not, by itself, a North Hills service
          area.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/work/scharmyn-park-toilets/">See the field restroom job</a></p>
        <aside class="todo">
          <p>
            <strong>TODO: confirm this list with Jerry.</strong>
            Draft only. These are neighborhoods and towns around Brookline and
            the South Hills. Do not publish them as a service area until he
            checks the names, adds any he wants, and crosses off the ones he
            does not cover.
          </p>
        </aside>
        <ul class="area-list">
          {draftTowns.map((town) => <li>{town} <span class="fine">· draft</span></li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <iframe
          class="map-frame"
          title="Map of the Pittsburgh 15226 area, including Brookline"
          src="https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-80.08%2C40.36%2C-79.96%2C40.43&amp;layer=mapnik"
          loading="lazy"
        ></iframe>
        <p class="fine">
          Map of the Pittsburgh, PA 15226 area.
          <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/#map=13/40.394/-80.020">Open the map</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
